problems.problem:
The mole Črt has $6$ chambers in his burrow, numbered with the numbers from $1$ to $6$. Between some of them Črt has dug tunnels, so that from every chamber he can crawl through some tunnels to every other chamber. No two tunnels intersect. Every tunnel begins in some chamber, ends in some other chamber (different from the starting one), and does not pass through any chamber in between. Two chambers that are directly connected by a tunnel are called adjacent. List the pairs of adjacent chambers if the following holds:
- if Črt crawls through exactly three (not necessarily distinct) tunnels, he can get from chamber $1$ to chambers $1$ and $6$;
- if Črt crawls through exactly three (not necessarily distinct) tunnels, he cannot get from chamber $1$ to chamber $2$;
- if Črt crawls through exactly four (not necessarily distinct) tunnels, he cannot get from chamber $1$ to chamber $6$;
- if Črt crawls through exactly two tunnels, he cannot get from chamber $1$ to chamber $5$.
